+## 9. Replay run plan: config A and B choice (round 2, 2026-10-12)
+
+**Config A** = `--spec-type ngram-mod` at the documented defaults
+(`--spec-ngram-mod-n-min 48 --spec-ngram-mod-n-max 64 --spec-ngram-mod-n-match 24`
+per §2). This is the ngram variant already probed in `docs/engine-review.md`
+(162 tok/s on repeated text, +4 MiB VRAM, zero on a fresh prompt) and the only
+ngram backend with a prior data point, so it is the primary deploy candidate.
+
+**Config B** = `--spec-type ngram-mod --spec-ngram-mod-n-min 64
+--spec-ngram-mod-n-max 128` (wider ngram window 64-128 vs A's 48-64). Choice:
+
+- *Proven mechanism, not an untested algorithm.* ngram-mod already drafts tokens
+  in prior testing, so B is a clean one-variable sensitivity test. The only other
+  untested ngram backend is `ngram-cache`; running it risks a full ~100-min slot
+  on a config that may draft 0 tokens with no prior signal, so it is held for a
+  follow-up rather than burned as B.
+- *The window-width axis is the actionable one.* Real agent traffic re-emits long
+  file contents, diffs and test output (see §7 cache_n growth), so the benefit of
+  ngram self-speculation lives in matching *long* spans. A wider lookup window
+  (64-128) is the single change most likely to lift the dual-slot tok/s, and it
+  gives a direct deploy candidate either way: if B (wide) beats A (default) on
+  dual-agent greedy, the wide window is the deploy config; if A wins, the default
+  ngram-mod is.
+- *Same backend, same defaults everywhere else*, so A vs B isolates exactly the
+  window-width variable.
+
+**mmproj outcome:** *to be confirmed empirically* once A and B run on :8089 —
+§3's static verdict (speculation usable with `--mmproj` loaded, text-only
+traffic) is confirmed if A/B report `draft_n > 0` / `draft_n_accepted > 0` on
+foreground rows (with the fork's timings omitting these fields only when nothing
+was drafted, §3/§7; a whole-arm zero means spec is off or the ngram never
+matched, and the server log then distinguishes refusal from no-match).
+`bench/spec_replay.py` aborts on a stale :8089 before Popen and falls back to
+`-nommproj` only on a genuine spec refusal (log match on §3's gate lines).
+This section will be updated with the actual `draft_n` evidence after the
+A-greedy and B-greedy runs land in `bench/results/*/m1-ngram/replay/`.
+
